CHAPTER.VERS:
For thus says Yahweh to the men of Judah and to Jerusalem, Break up your

          {+}
         fallow ground, and don't sow among thorns.

Circumcise yourselves to Yahweh, and take away the foreskins of your

          {+}
         heart, you

          {+}
         men of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem; or else my wrath will go forth like fire, and burn so that none can quench it, because of the evil of your

          {+}
         doings.

Declare

          {+}
         in Judah, and publish in Jerusalem; and say, Blow

          {+}
         the trumpet in the land: cry aloud and say, Assemble yourselves, and let us go into the fortified cities.

Then I said, Ah, Sovereign Yahweh! Surely you have greatly deceived this people and Jerusalem, saying, You

          {+}
         will have peace; whereas the sword reaches to the life.
